{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sigāla’s Father","html":"<article id='thag1.18'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.18 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.18 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Siṅgālapituttheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sigāla’s Father </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ahu buddhassa dāyādo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>There was an heir of the Buddha, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhikkhu bhesakaḷāvane; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a monk in Bhesakaḷā forest, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kevalaṁ aṭṭhisaññāya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who suffused the entire earth </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>apharī pathaviṁ imaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>with the perception of bones. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Maññehaṁ kāmarāgaṁ so, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I think he will quickly </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>khippameva pahissatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>get rid of sensual desire. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Siṅgālapitā thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
